<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib">

    <!-- Linux app strings - ENGLISH. Only keys present here are overridden; anything omitted falls back to LinuxStrings.en.xaml. -->

    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.PressKey">Press a key…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.NotSet">Not set</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.KeyRefused">That key can't be used</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.FolderNote">Left empty, the logs are looked for in the Steam (Proton) folder of EVE Online.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.ImportTitle">Settings from the Windows app</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.ImportPick">Choose the Windows app's EVE MultiPreview.json</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.Import">Import settings from Windows…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.ImportFile">Settings file</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.ImportBad">Not imported: that is not a readable EVE MultiPreview settings file.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.ImportFailed">Not imported: the file could not be copied.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.ImportDone">Imported. The old settings are in</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.ResizeNote">To resize a thumbnail, hold the right mouse button on it, press the left button too and move the mouse. Every thumbnail follows; hold Ctrl to resize only that one.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.Hidden">Hidden</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.NoCharacters">No characters yet. They appear here once an EVE client is running.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.GroupNameUsed">Type a name no group uses yet.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.GroupNext">Next key</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.GroupPrevious">Previous key</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.GroupMembers">Members</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.Notifications">Desktop notifications</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.SpeechDefaultVoice">the system's default voice</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.SpeechNoProgram">No speech program found, so nothing can be spoken. Install speech-dispatcher (spd-say) or espeak-ng.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.SpeechTryFailed">The voice could not say that. Check that speech-dispatcher or espeak-ng works and that a sound device is connected.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.PushDpapi">The saved link comes from the Windows app, where it is encrypted for that Windows user. It can't be read here: paste it again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.PushKeptIn">The link is kept in a file only you can read: {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.PushWriteFailed">The link could not be saved: its file could not be written.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.PushAwayNote">Away is read from the X server's idle time. Where the X server can't say, alerts are sent anyway.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.HotkeyClash">Same key as: {0}. Only one of them gets it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.HistOff">The alert history is switched off, so new alerts are not kept. Switch it on under Settings › Alerts › History.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.HistNoDialog">This desktop has no file dialog, so the file was saved in the settings folder.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.NotifyOn">Show desktop notifications</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.NotifyOn.Desc">Each alert you choose below shows a notification, with buttons to switch to that client or to snooze the alert for 15 minutes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.EndFrozenRefused">MultiPreview could not end {0}'s client.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.ClosedNote">Client closed unexpectedly is not available on Linux: Linux does not tell MultiPreview how a client it did not start ended, so a crash looks the same as quitting.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.CommandsTitle">Commands from other programs</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.AcceptCommands.Desc">Lets a Stream Deck app, a desktop shortcut or a script tell the running MultiPreview to bring a character to the front, switch profile, or toggle thumbnails or focus mode. Only programs of your own account can.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.CommandsNote">Run MultiPreview again with a command, for example below; a Stream Deck app (StreamController, streamdeck-ui, OpenDeck) runs it from a button. eve-multipreview --help lists every command.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.UpdateNotWritable">MultiPreview's folder can't be written by your account. Download the new version from the release page.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.NotYet">Not available on Linux yet: {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.VolumeDesc">Each client's volume on this desktop's sound server. A client remembers it for next time.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.ResizeAllDesc">Width × height. Apply to all resizes every thumbnail where it is, and new thumbnails start at this size.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.LookGallery.Desc">One click changes the settings window and its dialogs at once. The thumbnails stay as they are.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.LookHelp.Body">Each card shows a small preview of a look; one click picks it. The settings window and its dialogs change at once; nothing has to restart. The thumbnails, their menus and the desktop notifications stay as they are.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Classic** is the navy of the old settings window. **Windows 11** is the dark look of Windows 11's own Settings. **High contrast** is black and white, with larger text. The other nine have their own colours and type, and **Capsule**, **Blueprint**, **Ink** and **Terminal** also lay out the page their own way.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.LookThemeSection">Desktop light and dark</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.LookFollowTheme">Show Daylight while the desktop's style is light</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.LookFollowTheme.Desc">Dark, no preference, or a desktop that does not say shows the look you picked. The look you pick stays saved.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.LookThemeOn">The desktop's style is light, so Daylight is shown. The look you pick is kept and shows when the desktop goes dark, or now if you turn the switch off.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.LookThemeHelp.Title">Desktop light and dark</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Linux.LookThemeHelp.Body">With **Show Daylight while the desktop's style is light** on, MultiPreview shows **Daylight** whenever your desktop asks apps for a light style (the light or dark setting of GNOME, KDE Plasma and other desktops that tell apps through the freedesktop settings portal), and the look you picked when it is dark. A change on the desktop shows at once, without a restart.&#x0A;&#x0A;Your pick is never overwritten: it stays saved and shows again when the desktop goes dark or when you turn the switch off. If the desktop does not say, your own look shows. The switch is off by default and changes the settings window only, not the thumbnails.</sys:String>

</ResourceDictionary>
